{
  "id": "fluency-l7-evaluating",
  "lesson": "l7-evaluating",
  "title": "Fluency: definite integrals",
  "n": 20,
  "pass": 0.9,
  "minutes": 12,
  "families": [
    {
      "id": "power",
      "weight": 2,
      "skill": "evaluate the integral of a power",
      "vars": {
        "k": { "int": [1, 3] },
        "m": { "int": [-2, 2], "not": [0] },
        "p": { "int": [-2, 3] },
        "q": { "int": [-2, 3] }
      },
      "let": { "k1": "k + 1", "c": "m*(k + 1)", "fq": "m*q^(k + 1)", "fp": "m*p^(k + 1)", "ans": "m*(q^(k + 1) - p^(k + 1))" },
      "where": ["p != q", "ans != 0"],
      "prompt": "Evaluate $\\int_{{{p}}}^{{{q}}} {mono(x; c, k)}\\,dx$.",
      "widget": { "kind": "numeric", "answer": "{ans}", "tol": { "abs": 0 } },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "limits-swapped", "value": "{-ans}", "line": "You worked out $F({p}) - F({q})$. The top limit goes first: $F({q}) - F({p})$." },
        { "id": "no-divide", "value": "{c*(q^k1 - p^k1)}", "line": "You raised the power to {k1} but did not divide by {k1}." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "An antiderivative is $F(x) = {mono(x; m, k1)}$.",
        "$F({q}) - F({p}) = {fq} - {fp:()} = {ans}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "quadratic",
      "weight": 2,
      "skill": "evaluate the integral of a quadratic",
      "vars": {
        "a": { "int": [-3, 3], "not": [0] },
        "h": { "int": [-3, 3] },
        "c": { "int": [-5, 5] },
        "p": { "int": [-2, 2] },
        "q": { "int": [-1, 3] }
      },
      "let": {
        "b": "2*h",
        "fq": "a*q^3/3 + h*q^2 + c*q",
        "fp": "a*p^3/3 + h*p^2 + c*p",
        "ans": "a*(q^3 - p^3)/3 + h*(q^2 - p^2) + c*(q - p)",
        "nodiv": "a*(q^3 - p^3) + 2*h*(q^2 - p^2) + c*(q - p)"
      },
      "where": ["p < q", "ans != 0", "nodiv != ans", "nodiv != -ans"],
      "prompt": "Evaluate $\\int_{{{p}}}^{{{q}}} ({poly(x; a, b, c)})\\,dx$. Give a fraction or a decimal.",
      "widget": { "kind": "numeric", "answer": "{ans}", "tol": { "abs": 0.0005 }, "accept": "${ans:frac}$, or a decimal within 0.0005" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "limits-swapped", "value": "{-ans}", "tol": { "abs": 0.0005 }, "line": "You worked out $F({p}) - F({q})$. The top limit goes first: $F({q}) - F({p})$." },
        { "id": "no-divide", "value": "{nodiv}", "tol": { "abs": 0.0005 }, "line": "You raised each power by one but did not divide by the new power." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "An antiderivative is $F(x) = {poly(x; a/3, h, c, 0)}$.",
        "$F({q}) = {fq:frac}$ and $F({p}) = {fp:frac}$.",
        "So the integral is $F({q}) - F({p}) = {ans:frac}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "reciprocal-square",
      "weight": 1,
      "skill": "evaluate the integral of a negative power",
      "vars": {
        "c": { "int": [1, 12] },
        "p": { "int": [1, 5] },
        "q": { "int": [2, 6] }
      },
      "let": { "ans": "c*(1/p - 1/q)", "low": "c*(1/p^3 - 1/q^3)/3" },
      "where": ["p < q"],
      "prompt": "Evaluate $\\displaystyle\\int_{{{p}}}^{{{q}}} \\frac{{{c}}}{{x^2}}\\,dx$. Give a fraction or a decimal.",
      "widget": { "kind": "numeric", "answer": "{ans}", "tol": { "abs": 0.0005 }, "accept": "${ans:frac}$, or a decimal within 0.0005" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "sign-lost", "value": "{-ans}", "tol": { "abs": 0.0005 }, "line": "An antiderivative of $x^{{-2}}$ is $-x^{{-1}}$: the new power is $-1$, so the sign flips." },
        { "id": "power-lowered", "value": "{low}", "tol": { "abs": 0.0005 }, "line": "You lowered the power to $-3$. Raise it by one, to $-1$." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "An antiderivative is $F(x) = -\\frac{{{c}}}{{x}}$.",
        "$F({q}) - F({p}) = {-c/q:frac} - ({-c/p:frac}) = {ans:frac}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "exponential",
      "weight": 1,
      "skill": "evaluate the integral of an exponential",
      "vars": {
        "c": { "int": [1, 9] },
        "kq": { "pick": [[1, 2], [1, 3], [-1, 1], [-1, 2], [-1, 3], [2, 1], [2, 2], [-2, 1], [-2, 2], [0.5, 3], [0.5, 4], [-0.5, 2], [-0.5, 3], [-0.5, 4]], "as": ["k", "q"] },
        "v": { "pick": ["x", "t"] }
      },
      "let": {
        "r": "c/k",
        "kqq": "k*q",
        "ans": "c/k*(exp(k*q) - 1)",
        "top": "c/k*exp(k*q)",
        "nodiv": "c*(exp(k*q) - 1)"
      },
      "where": ["abs(top - nodiv) > 0.002"],
      "prompt": "Evaluate $\\int_{{0}}^{{{q}}} {c:c}e^{{{k:c}{v}}}\\,d{v}$, to 3 decimal places.",
      "widget": { "kind": "numeric", "answer": "{ans}", "tol": { "abs": 0.00051 }, "accept": "${r:cfrac}(e^{{{kqq}}} - 1) \\approx {ans:dp3}$" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "lower-limit-zero", "value": "{top}", "tol": { "abs": 0.00051 }, "line": "You stopped at $F({q})$. Subtract $F(0)$ as well: $e^0 = 1$, not 0." },
        { "id": "no-divide", "value": "{nodiv}", "tol": { "abs": 0.00051 }, "line": "An antiderivative of $e^{{{k:c}{v}}}$ is $\\dfrac{{e^{{{k:c}{v}}}}}{{{k}}}$: divide by {k}.", "when": "k != 1 and k != -1" },
        { "id": "sign-lost", "value": "{-ans}", "tol": { "abs": 0.00051 }, "line": "Dividing by ${k}$ makes the factor in front negative: you lost its sign.", "when": "k < 0" }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "An antiderivative is $F({v}) = {r:cfrac}e^{{{k:c}{v}}}$.",
        "$F({q}) - F(0) = {r:cfrac}(e^{{{kqq}}} - 1) \\approx {ans:dp3}$."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
